.EE
.IP
.EX
#ifndef CBOR_NESTING_DEPTH_DEFAULT
#define CBOR_NESTING_DEPTH_DEFAULT 128
#endif

#ifndef CBOR_STRING_LENGTH_DEFAULT
#define CBOR_STRING_LENGTH_DEFAULT SIZE_MAX
#endif

#ifndef CBOR_CONTAINER_ELEMENTS_DEFAULT
#define CBOR_CONTAINER_ELEMENTS_DEFAULT SIZE_MAX
#endif

\f[B]struct\f[R] limits {
    static \f[B]constexpr\f[R] std::size_t nesting_depth = CBOR_NESTING_DEPTH_DEFAULT;
    static \f[B]constexpr\f[R] std::size_t string_length = CBOR_STRING_LENGTH_DEFAULT;
    static \f[B]constexpr\f[R] std::size_t container_elements = CBOR_CONTAINER_ELEMENTS_DEFAULT;
};
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
The error values of the library, their conversion to
\f[CR]std::error_code\f[R], and the limits of a build.
.SS cbor::error
The fault that a call returns in its
\f[CR]std::expected<T, cbor::error>\f[R].
Bad input never throws.
The first value is 1.
So a \f[CR]std::error_code\f[R] from a \f[CR]cbor::error\f[R] is always
true as a \f[CR]bool\f[R].
A wrong use of the library is not an error value: it does not compile,
or it throws \f[CR]std::logic_error\f[R].
.PP
